      "content": "## Test Case: [TC-004] Remember Me — Session Persists Across Browser Restart\n\n**Type:** Functional\n**Priority:** High\n\n### Preconditions\n- Registered user account exists: `test@demo.com` / `Test1234!`\n- Browser has no existing session cookie for the application\n\n### Test Steps\n| Step | Action | Expected Result |\n|------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Navigate to `/login` | Login page is displayed |\n| 2 | Enter valid email and password | Fields populated |\n| 3 | Check the \"Remember me\" checkbox | Checkbox is selected |\n| 4 | Click \"Sign In\" | User is redirected to `/dashboard`; a persistent auth token is set in the browser (cookie `max-age` ≥ 30 days) |\n| 5 | Close the browser completely and reopen it | Browser starts a fresh session |\n| 6 | Navigate to `/dashboard` | User is still authenticated; redirected to `/dashboard` without being prompted to log in again |\n| 7 | Inspect the auth token expiry | Token expiry is `createdAt + 30 days` (±1 minute tolerance) |\n\n### Expected Outcome\nUser remains authenticated after a full browser restart; the auth token has a 30-day TTL and is not a session-only cookie.\n\n---",
