      "content": "## Test Case: [TC-006] Login with Non-Existent Email\n\n**Type:** Negative\n**Priority:** High\n\n### Preconditions\n- No account registered under `notregistered@demo.com`\n\n### Test Steps\n| Step | Action | Expected Result |\n|------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Navigate to `/login` | Login page displayed |\n| 2 | Enter `notregistered@demo.com` in the email field | Field populated |\n| 3 | Enter any password (e.g. `AnyPass1!`) | Field populated |\n| 4 | Click \"Sign In\" | Error message **\"Invalid email or password\"** is displayed; user remains on `/login` |\n| 5 | Verify response time | Response arrives in the same time window as a failed-password response (timing must not reveal whether the email exists) |\n\n### Expected Outcome\nThe application returns the same generic error for a non-existent email as for a wrong password, preventing user enumeration. Response timing does not leak existence of the account.\n\n---",
