      "content": "## Test Case: [TC-007] Login Form Submission with Empty Fields\n\n**Type:** Negative\n**Priority:** Medium\n\n### Preconditions\n- None\n\n### Test Steps\n| Step | Action | Expected Result |\n|------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Navigate to `/login` | Login page displayed |\n| 2 | Leave both email and password blank; click \"Sign In\" | Client-side validation fires; submission is blocked; both fields are highlighted as required |\n| 3 | Enter a valid email only, leave password blank; click \"Sign In\" | Submission blocked; password field highlighted as required |\n| 4 | Leave email blank, enter a password; click \"Sign In\" | Submission blocked; email field highlighted as required |\n| 5 | Confirm no HTTP request is sent for any of the above | Network tab shows no POST to `/api/auth/login` |\n\n### Expected Outcome\nThe form enforces presence validation client-side; no login request reaches the backend when mandatory fields are empty.\n\n---",
