      "content": "## Test Case: [TC-008] SQL Injection and XSS Attempts in Login Fields\n\n**Type:** Security\n**Priority:** Critical\n\n### Preconditions\n- The application is deployed in a test environment with server-side logging accessible\n- Registered user: `test@demo.com` / `Test1234!`\n\n### Test Steps\n| Step | Action | Expected Result |\n|------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Navigate to `/login` | Login page displayed |\n| 2 | Enter `' OR '1'='1' --` in the email field; enter any password; click \"Sign In\" | Response is \"Invalid email or password\"; user is NOT authenticated; no SQL error or stack trace exposed |\n| 3 | Enter `<script>alert('xss')</script>` in the email field; any password; click \"Sign In\" | Script is not executed; value is escaped in any reflected output; response is the standard error message |\n| 4 | Enter `admin@demo.com'--` in email; any password; click \"Sign In\" | Standard error; not authenticated |\n| 5 | Check server logs | No unhandled exceptions or raw SQL errors logged; all inputs are parameterised or sanitised |\n\n### Expected Outcome\nAll injection payloads are treated as plain strings. No authentication bypass, script execution, or internal error disclosure occurs.\n\n---",
