      "content": "## Test Case: [TC-009] Lockout Counter Resets After Successful Login\n\n**Type:** Edge Case\n**Priority:** High\n\n### Preconditions\n- Registered user: `test@demo.com` / `Test1234!`\n- No prior failed attempts on the account\n\n### Test Steps\n| Step | Action | Expected Result |\n|------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Attempt login with wrong password **4 times** | Each attempt shows \"Invalid email or password\" |\n| 2 | Log in with the **correct** password | User is authenticated; redirected to `/dashboard` |\n| 3 | Log out | User returned to `/login` |\n| 4 | Attempt login with wrong password **4 more times** | Each attempt shows \"Invalid email or password\" (counter has reset to 0 after successful login) |\n| 5 | Attempt login with wrong password a **5th time** | Shows \"Invalid email or password\" — account is NOT locked yet (counter is at 5 cumulative *since last success*, so the 6th would lock) |\n| 6 | Attempt login with correct credentials | User logs in successfully |\n\n### Expected Outcome\nA successful login resets the failed-attempt counter. Prior failures before a successful login do not carry over and contribute to lockout.\n\n---",
